{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Your fullness.</b> A designation for wine; and your tear, a designation for oil. The Gaon [Saadia] said that the word מלאתך includes both the fullness of grain and the fullness of the vat, and said that דמעך hints at oil, because when the olive is pressed it descends in drops like a tear. Now he explained this verse in another place, namely: \"The first of your grain, your wine, and your oil\" (Deuteronomy 18:4). Therefore after it: \"the firstborn of your sons you shall give to Me,\" for he is the first of his strength. And Ben Zuta said that מלאתך refers to pregnancy, and דמעך is a designation for the emission of seed, which is the drop, and said: do not delay — that he should not delay taking a wife; therefore after it: \"the firstborn of your sons you shall give to Me.\" And this is madness. Why did he mention מלאתך before דמעך? For דמעך according to his opinion is the pouring of seed into the woman, and afterward pregnancy comes — and furthermore, the matter of pregnancy is not in man's hand but in HaShem's alone. Yefet said: this verse is mentioned so that one not delay the poor person from giving what he owes; thus shall you do to give the firstborn to the priest."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:31.625177093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}